{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/952940-werewolves-and-religion","id":952940,"title":"Werewolves and Religion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-17T19:46:04-07:00","id":952940,"title":"Werewolves and Religion","content":"alright I have been doing some tinkering with the werewolves for my Old World Of Darkness setting (yes I use the Forsaken because I like them better than the Garou) and I have come up with an idea that could work for a new and old world. A possible lodge or multi pack belief that equates Luna to the Virgin Mary. This belief was popularized by werewolves of Christian upbringings in the dark ages to reconcile their faith with their new lives after the first change. I did this for a dark ages game which I used the Forsaken as NPC's in Bishops Lin in England. I have been doing this with some other faiths, Paganism I find to be easier than the Judeo-Christian faith in reconciling their beliefs. The intention though of equating Christian faith with the werewolf creation myth is redemption from mother luna. The belief is that Mary was either possessed by a Lune or an avatar of Luna herself. Of course this is up to interpenetration and like all faith I do not have it be factual. I would like to hear any input on this and if any of you had done something similar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T19:53:00-07:00","id":952942,"title":"","content":"<br /> Look up the Benandanti/ Hounds of God, they were a fertility cult from eastern Europe (and parts of Germany and Italy) it's a pretty interesting look at Christian werewolves. And by interesting I mean Drunken Chaotic Good Werewolf Paladins of Jesus. Seriously. The earlier folktales portray them more seriously, but in later years they became somewhat buffoonish heroes. The guys on the first tongue translation thread even created a word for one of the stories about them, <i>sketuth</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-17-2016, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T20:02:33-07:00","id":952944,"title":"","content":"Reconciling faith with reality is one thing.<br /> <br /> Trying to mesh two different mythologies together is another.<br /> <br /> These days, I find the former to be far more interesting than the latter. Like... I do not need Jesus to be a werewolf (for example). He can be God incarnated as Man, or the second-to-last prophet, as per existing claims, just fine. It's just more interesting to have a werewolf, who must hunt, who has to negotiate between the spirit world and the Flesh, and also believes that he must follow Jesus, who brings not peace but a sword, but also tells him to turn the other cheek sometimes, who tells him to root out the plank in his own eye before he gets whiny about everyone else, and if his right hand causes him to sin, he will seriously chop it off and regrow it after a few weeks because that shit needed purifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T20:07:56-07:00","id":952947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/952940-werewolves-and-religion?p=952942#post952942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look up the Benandanti/ Hounds of God, they were a fertility cult from eastern Europe (and parts of Germany and Italy) it's a pretty interesting look at Christian werewolves. And by interesting I mean Drunken Chaotic Good Werewolf Paladins of Jesus. Seriously. The earlier folktales portray them more seriously, but in later years they became somewhat buffoonish heroes. The guys on the first tongue translation thread even created a word for one of the stories about them, <i>sketuth</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting thank you for telling me about them I may have to use them in a future game set in Eastern Europe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T20:21:14-07:00","id":952952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/952940-werewolves-and-religion?p=952944#post952944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reconciling faith with reality is one thing.<br /> <br /> Trying to mesh two different mythologies together is another.<br /> <br /> These days, I find the former to be far more interesting than the latter. Like... I do not need Jesus to be a werewolf (for example). He can be God incarnated as Man, or the second-to-last prophet, as per existing claims, just fine. It's just more interesting to have a werewolf, who must hunt, who has to negotiate between the spirit world and the Flesh, and also believes that he must follow Jesus, who brings not peace but a sword, but also tells him to turn the other cheek sometimes, who tells him to root out the plank in his own eye before he gets whiny about everyone else, and if his right hand causes him to sin, he will seriously chop it off and regrow it after a few weeks because that shit needed purifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well interesting idea. I still think that there would be those who try and mesh faiths together. But thank you for the input","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T21:16:59-07:00","id":952969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/952940-werewolves-and-religion?p=952947#post952947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very interesting thank you for telling me about them I may have to use them in a future game set in Eastern Europe</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, keep in mind that Saint Christopher is often portrayed as having a canine head. And there's also an Irish tale about a werewolf couple where the wife is dying and a priest gives them last rites that you might want to look up,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T21:41:46-07:00","id":952977,"title":"","content":"You might check out the lodge of the Savior, in Lodges the Faithful. They are Christian werewolves who see a lot of parallels between the legends of the bible and those of the Uratha.<br /> <br /> I usually see Esau associated with werewolves, but that's another bible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:33:50-07:00","id":953322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/952940-werewolves-and-religion?p=952952#post952952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well interesting idea. I still think that there would be those who try and mesh faiths together. But thank you for the input</div> </div> </div> </div>That's literally how cults and religions evolve. Check out the origins of Christmas, for example. Everybody has subjective view about their belief, and people exposed to several points of view often seek to reconcile them.<br /> <br /> @OP Which edition are you handling? The setting is primarily built on WoD or ChroD?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:04:43-07:00","id":953605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/952940-werewolves-and-religion?p=953322#post953322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's literally how cults and religions evolve. Check out the origins of Christmas, for example. Everybody has subjective view about their belief, and people exposed to several points of view often seek to reconcile them.<br /> <br /> @OP Which edition are you handling? The setting is primarily built on WoD or ChroD?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am doing it in WoD currently, but I am going to to it for CHroD as well. I am using 2nd edition Forsaken primarily","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:07:48-07:00","id":953607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/952940-werewolves-and-religion?p=952977#post952977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might check out the lodge of the Savior, in Lodges the Faithful. They are Christian werewolves who see a lot of parallels between the legends of the bible and those of the Uratha.<br /> <br /> I usually see Esau associated with werewolves, but that's another bible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually forgot about them, I may have to bring them in now for my Jazz age game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:29:27-07:00","id":953625,"title":"","content":"There's a Fire-Touched preacher in <i>Night Horrors: Wolfsbane</i> who may well wind up being the big bad in the chronicle I'm running. He hasn't shown up in my Actual Play yet, but I had SO MUCH FUN running him when some of the PCs sat in on one of his sermons. I ad-libbed, and didn't get a chance to write much down, but I went ALL OUT with parallels between Father Wolf and Jesus. Something like this:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The BEASTS that rose up against THE LORD wrought a terrible curse on the land and on themselves! And it has endured for generation upon generation, brothers and sisters! You know it, don't you? Can I get an 'amen'? They who SLEW THEIR FATHER tore the world in two with their sin, and we who came later suffer under that burden still! But all is not lost, brothers and sisters! All is not lost! For the LORD, even as he was led into destruction by treacherous dogs, he prophesied that there would always be a faithful remnant! There would always be a PURE AND HOLY LINE upon the earth, who would NOT fall to temptation and sin! Who would WITNESS HIS TRUTH and HUNT THE WICKED for the damage they have done!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I had one player who's read quite a bit of the book, and the looks he was giving me! #priceless","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:01:49-07:00","id":958370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/952940-werewolves-and-religion?p=953625#post953625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Fire-Touched preacher in <i>Night Horrors: Wolfsbane</i> who may well wind up being the big bad in the chronicle I'm running. He hasn't shown up in my Actual Play yet, but I had SO MUCH FUN running him when some of the PCs sat in on one of his sermons. I ad-libbed, and didn't get a chance to write much down, but I went ALL OUT with parallels between Father Wolf and Jesus. Something like this:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The BEASTS that rose up against THE LORD wrought a terrible curse on the land and on themselves! And it has endured for generation upon generation, brothers and sisters! You know it, don't you? Can I get an 'amen'? They who SLEW THEIR FATHER tore the world in two with their sin, and we who came later suffer under that burden still! But all is not lost, brothers and sisters! All is not lost! For the LORD, even as he was led into destruction by treacherous dogs, he prophesied that there would always be a faithful remnant! There would always be a PURE AND HOLY LINE upon the earth, who would NOT fall to temptation and sin! Who would WITNESS HIS TRUTH and HUNT THE WICKED for the damage they have done!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I had one player who's read quite a bit of the book, and the looks he was giving me! #priceless</div> </div> </div> </div>That is awesome, I am thinking of doing something similar in a upcoming vampire the dark ages session, the city of Lin is controlled by the Iron Masters who have drawn a parallel between Luna and Mary Magdalen and Red Wolf as a representation of Christ. So I am thinking of one of the packs being made up of priests and during the feast the pc's are invited to by the leader of the Iron Masters in Ely they are going to hear a prayer before the feast<br /> &quot;Oh great Mother Luna, you who watch over us, you who empower us, you who we shall find redemption from. We are gathered here to feast on this bounty you have brought before us and we pray to you for guidance in these troubled times. For our enemies howl at our gates and even our own brothers wish us death for our faith in you and Christ. But like Christ we shall forgive our enemies for their folly and pray for their souls redemption. Bless us this night oh Luna, lead us to redemption. Amen&quot;<br /> This faith in Christianity that the Iron Masters of Lin cling to goes very deep to the point of equating other Tribe founders as saints. This has caused many problems in the Isles for the Iron Masters because the majority follow this heresy, while many Blood Talons cling on to Odinism or other forms of martial Paganism. The Fire-Touched of course see this as blatant heresy for equating their tribal founder to Christ is revolting in their eyes, the Predator Kings see the use of Religion to begin with as taint because it was created by humans, and the Ivory Claws are angered the Iron Masters have enough power in the church on the Isles to rival the Vampires, that and the Masters are trying to find some common ground with the Cainites so they can hopefully wipe out the Pure. That and the Northern Iron masters who also cling onto the old pagan faiths of the Isles are angered that these Norman Iron Masters are trying to convert the Pagans of the North which is causing more conflict within the Tribe over faith and religion and soon will cause violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T18:52:59-07:00","id":959616,"title":"","content":"Nice - some very nifty ideas there! A game of Iron Masters battling Ivory Claws and vampires for influence within the medieval Church would be hella fun! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T21:51:09-07:00","id":959661,"title":"","content":"In the Hunting Grounds: Spain I'm currently writing, I've done something similar.<br /> <br /> The Lodge of Saviour is very strong in Spain, but they are divided by theological reasons:<br /> - One faction (the Lunists) believes than Virgin Mary is a manifestation of Luna. They even think than the myth of the apparition of the Virgin in Covadonga (the legendary beginnings of the Reconquista) was a real manifestation of Luna. Some of them are also allied with a faction of Baal-Hadad who identifies Helios with the judeo-christian God (so, Jesus Christ, in this theology would be the son of Helios and Luna).<br /> - Another faction (the MarIanists) sees this as heresy. They are more &quot;orthodox&quot; catholics (for the werewolves standards), who try to mantain apart the Uratha and the Catholics myths. They believe than Mary and Luna are two different beings, and than maybe Mary, as the Mother of God, might have ascended to an status even higher than Luna.<br /> <br /> I also have created for Spain the Crusaders of Santiago, a Lodge founded by a spirit of Reconquista in Middle Ages, but that has became the main Lodge of the country. That Spirit, the Sword of the Prophet, has grown in power since then, and currently has became the Spirit of Spain itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 08-29-2016, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T22:05:36-07:00","id":959668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/952940-werewolves-and-religion?p=952952#post952952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well interesting idea. I still think that there would be those who try and mesh faiths together. But thank you for the input</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm sure there are those who have tried. It's not like they undergo the first change and suddenly decide <i>&quot;Well, I'm a werewolf. Time to change my religious beliefs over night!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T22:18:40-07:00","id":959671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/952940-werewolves-and-religion?p=959661#post959661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Hunting Grounds: Spain I'm currently writing, I've done something similar.<br /> <br /> The Lodge of Saviour is very strong in Spain, but they are divided by theological reasons:<br /> - One faction (the Lunists) believes than Virgin Mary is a manifestation of Luna. They even think than the myth of the apparition of the Virgin in Covadonga (the legendary beginnings of the Reconquista) was a real manifestation of Luna. Some of them are also allied with a faction of Baal-Hadad who identifies Helios with the judeo-christian God (so, Jesus Christ, in this theology would be the son of Helios and Luna).<br /> - Another faction (the MarIanists) sees this as heresy. They are more &quot;orthodox&quot; catholics (for the werewolves standards), who try to mantain apart the Uratha and the Catholics myths. They believe than Mary and Luna are two different beings, and than maybe Mary, as the Mother of God, might have ascended to an status even higher than Luna.<br /> <br /> I also have created for Spain the Crusaders of Santiago, a Lodge founded by a spirit of Reconquista in Middle Ages, but that has became the main Lodge of the country. That Spirit, the Sword of the Prophet, has grown in power since then, and currently has became the Spirit of Spain itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really neat, I especially like the rift. Is it bloody or more of a cold tension?<br /> <br /> I hope you're willing to share the Hunting Ground if you finish it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-29-2016, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T23:38:29-07:00","id":959689,"title":"","content":"It's more a cold war. The Lunists are more prevalent in the Cantabric coast (North) and the Meseta (Central Spain) territories. The Marianists are more prevalent in the Mediterranean territories and the South of Spain. Although in the past there were some fightings, a local Saviours Council decreed that both viewpoints were acceptable (although the most fanatical of both sides consider heretics the other ones). Also, the war against the Pure in Spain (the so called Segunda Reconquista) forces them to work together.<br /> <br /> Of course I'll share it when I finish it. It'll be two books. One for Spain in general, and another one for its Territories. The content o the first one is finished, although I must update it to 2nd Edition (and I think I'll add a bloody war among Saviours in the past). And I'm still writing the second one. The main problem is that it'll be in Spanish, but if someone wats to translate it I'll be pleased to share the original files.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}